&TRACE OFF
***********************************************************************
*   Syntax:                                                           *
*   FORCE ALL    EXCEPT userid1 userid2 ... useridn                   *
*         userid                                                      *
*                                                                     *
*   EXTERNAL REFERENCES                                               *
*   NONE                                                              *
*                                                                     *
*                                    Henry Nussbacher - July 1983     *
*                                                                     *
*               (c) Weizmann Institute of Science                     *
***********************************************************************
&BUFFER *
* THIS WILL READ IN THE WHOLE FILE FOR THE LOOK-A-SIDE BUFFER
&CALL -END_OF_FILE
&IF  &N LT 1       &GOTO -EXPLAIN
&IF .&1 NE .ALL    &GOTO -FORCE_SINGLE_USER
&IF .&2 NE .EXCEPT &GOTO -EXPLAIN
&IF .&3 EQ .       &GOTO -EXPLAIN
&TYPE Do you really wish to FORCE all users off the system?
&READ VAR &REPLY
&IF .&REPLY NE .YES &EXIT
***********************************************************************
*   USE THE NEXT LINE TO SPECIFY THE VM OPERATOR USERID, SO THAT      *
*   HE/SHE DOES NOT NEED TO BE SPECIFIED IN THE 'EXCEPT' LIST         *
***********************************************************************
&OPERATOR = VMOP
***********************************************************************
*   COMMENT OUT THE FOLLOWING LINE IF YOU DO NOT WISH TO DISABLE      *
*   ALL TERMINALS.  THOSE USERS AS SPECIFIED IN THE 'EXCEPT' LIST     *
*   WILL HAVE THEIR TERMINALS RE-ENABLED.                             *
***********************************************************************
CP DISABLE ALL
EXECIO * CP (STRING Q N
SENTRIES
* FIND OUT HOW MANY LINES OF 'Q N' TO PROCESS
&NUMBER_OF_LINES = &RC
&LINES = 1
* INITIALIZE THE NUMBER OF USERS TO PROCESS
&COUNT = 0
-Q_N_LOOP
***********************************************************************
*    &USER WILL BE OUR ARRAY OF USERS CURRENTLY LOGGED ON.            *
*    &DEVICE WILL BE AN ARRAY OF THE DEVICE ADDRESS LOGGED ON.        *
***********************************************************************
    &IF &LINES GT &NUMBER_OF_LINES &GOTO -BEGIN_PROCESSING
    &LINES = &LINES + 1
    &READ STRING  &LINE_OF_Q_N
    &COUNT = &COUNT + 1
    * MAXIMUM 4 USERS PER LINE OF 'Q N'
    &USER&COUNT  =  &SUBSTR OF &LINE_OF_Q_N  1 8
    &DEVICE&COUNT = &SUBSTR OF &LINE_OF_Q_N 12 3
    &COUNT = &COUNT + 1
    &USER&COUNT   = &SUBSTR OF &LINE_OF_Q_N 17 8
    &DEVICE&COUNT = &SUBSTR OF &LINE_OF_Q_N 28 3
    &COUNT = &COUNT + 1
    &USER&COUNT   = &SUBSTR OF &LINE_OF_Q_N 33 8
    &DEVICE&COUNT = &SUBSTR OF &LINE_OF_Q_N 44 3
    &COUNT = &COUNT + 1
    &USER&COUNT   = &SUBSTR OF &LINE_OF_Q_N 49 8
    &DEVICE&COUNT = &SUBSTR OF &LINE_OF_Q_N 60 3
&GOTO -Q_N_LOOP
-BEGIN_PROCESSING
&NUM = 1
&EXCEPTIONS = &N - 2
&LOOP -END &COUNT
***********************************************************************
*   BEGIN FORCING USERS OFF.                                          *
***********************************************************************
    &INNER_COUNT = 3
    &IF .&USER&NUM = . &EXIT
    &LOOP -LOOP_2 &EXCEPTIONS
          &IF .&USER&NUM EQ .&&INNER_COUNT &GOTO -EXCEPTION
          &IF .&USER&NUM EQ .&OPERATOR     &GOTO -EXCEPTION
          &INNER_COUNT = &INNER_COUNT + 1
    -LOOP_2
&TYPE Forcing &USER&NUM
CP FORCE &USER&NUM
&GOTO -INCREMENT
-EXCEPTION
&IF .&DEVICE&NUM = .DSC &GOTO -INCREMENT
&TYPE Re-enabling terminal &DEVICE&NUM for user &USER&NUM
CP ENABLE &DEVICE&NUM
-INCREMENT
&NUM = &NUM + 1
-END
CP Q N
&EXIT
***********************************************************************
-FORCE_SINGLE_USER
CP FORCE &1
&EXIT &RC
***********************************************************************
-EXPLAIN
&BEGTYPE -BEG_END
Syntax is:
          FORCE ALL    EXCEPT userid1 userid2 ... useridn
                userid

FORCE userid will invoke the standard CP command to log a user off the
system.  FORCE ALL will log all users off the system except for those
listed after the word EXCEPT.  In addition, the VM operator can be
defined in this EXEC to be bypassed all the time.  Another option
within this EXEC is to issue a DISABLE ALL when a FORCE ALL is done.
Those users as specified in the exception list will not have their
terminals disabled.
-BEG_END
&EXIT 4
-END_OF_FILE
***********************************************************************
*  TRICK TO IMPROVE EXEC-2 PERFORMANCE.  READ EXEC-2 REFERENCE MANUAL *
*  PAGE 12, UNDER THE &BUFFER DESCRIPTION.                            *
***********************************************************************
&RETURN
